for cipherdoc v1 0 w 03 the initi checklist draft depend on t001 through t006 and t010 a later prerequisit audit found the checklist still incomplet while t005 docker imag slim down cve work and t029 window code sign remain open and releas note were draft in parallel while gate stay open diana place a secur gate hold on the releas pend both t005 s docker slim down cve work and t029 s window defend smartscreen code sign the task remain activ with those two gate unresolv\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e97842848a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-21-Release-v1-Gates.md\", \"id\": \"d0ddf0dd50f07774\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29818332711586826, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11301238016552607, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73024887, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-21-Release-v1-Gates.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e97842848a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-21-Release-v1-Gates.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-21-Release-v1-Gates.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1139, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:27\", \"token_count\": 635, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-37\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Windows Signing Gap\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 09:14] Evan**: Windows Defender and SmartScreen are both flagging the build for pilot testers — unsigned binaries get treated as untrusted by default.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:13] Alice**: Is the missing code-signing certificate the actual blocker here?\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:14] Evan**: Yes. We still don't have one. Until we do, every pilot install is going to trip a warning at best, get blocked outright at worst.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:16] Diana**: Release blocker?\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:17] Bob**: Copy.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:18] Evan**: It stays open as far as I'm concerned — this isn't something we can work around on the engineering side, we need the certificate.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:59] Alice**: Let's keep it open on the release gate rather than pushing it off the board. I'll chase the certificate process.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 37 slack thread window sign gap channel releas date 2026 09 02 2026 09 02 09 14 evan window defend and smartscreen are both flag the build for pilot tester unsign binari get treat a untrust by default 2026 09 02 10 13 alic is the miss code sign certif the actual blocker here 2026 09 02 10 14 evan yes we still don t have one until we do everi pilot instal is go to trip a warn at best get block outright at worst 2026 09 02 10 16 diana releas blocker 2026 09 02 10 17 bob copi 2026 09 02 1018 evan it stay open a far a i m concern this isn t someth we can work around on the engin side we need the certif 2026 09 02 10 59 alic let s keep it open on the releas gate rather than push it off the board i ll chase the certif process\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e911fa1a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"id\": \"4223f88ffbddf892\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.297599084107695, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10989424158242148, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73557705, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e911fa1a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 927, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:53\", \"token_count\": 288, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Worker Management Decision\\n\\nRetrospective note on the concurrency block confirmed 2026-08-25. For large-scale redaction jobs, the batch API moved from a synchronous blocking loop to an `asyncio`-driven queue: a single producer walks the file system and pushes document tasks, while a fixed pool of async workers pulls from the queue and orchestrates I/O against the redaction engine, built on top of the already-completed multi-threaded worker pool (T026).\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Ordering & Race Risk\\n\\nBecause documents vary widely in size, workers finish out of order. When multiple workers append to the same shared results manifest concurrently, writes can interleave and corrupt the JSON structure.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Update: Confirmed I/O Race, Throughput Regression\\n\\nConcurrency testing on 2026-08-25 confirmed the race is real, not just theoretical: under concurrent load, the race condition measurably cuts batch throughput by roughly 10% compared to the expected async speedup, because workers end up retrying/serializing around the corrupted-write recovery path. This is now blocking further rollout of the async scheduler.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nT037 is **Blocked** on resolving the manifest-write race before the async scheduler can be considered production-ready; the throughput regression it causes depends directly on how the T026 worker pool's result-writing is serialized.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 worker manag decis retrospect note on the concurr block confirm 2026 08 25 for larg scale redact job the batch api move from a synchron block loop to an asyncio driven queue a singl produc walk the file system and push document task while a fix pool of async worker pull from the queue and orchestr i o against the redact engin built on top of the alreadi complet multi thread worker pool t026 sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 order race risk becaus document vari wide in size worker finish out of order when multipl worker append to the same share result manifest concurr write can interleav and corrupt the json structur sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 updat confirm i o race throughput regress concurr test on 2026 08 25 confirm the race is real not just theoret under concurr load the race condit measur cut batch throughpu