{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"question":"privacy compliance Sentry opt-out audit release blocker v1.0.0"},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"question":"privacy compliance Sentry opt-out audit release blocker v1.0.0"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Opt-Out Behaviour Designed\\n\\nThe CLI and API collect anonymous usage metrics (pages processed, OCR fallback rate) to help tune the detection engine. Setting `CIPHER_TELEMETRY=0`, or the equivalent GUI toggle, is designed to immediately stop all outbound telemetry traffic to the metrics endpoint.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Design-Time Issue Found and Patched: Pending-Queue Leak\\n\\nWhile designing the flag semantics, testing surfaced that the opt-out flag blocked network egress correctly, but the `TelemetryLogger` kept writing event payloads to a local SQLite queue regardless. That meant re-enabling telemetry later would flush the entire backlog accumulated during the opt-out period, including events the user believed were never being recorded. The logger was patched to a no-op backend when opted out, closing that gap before the flag semantics were finalized.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Verification (Retrospective)\\n\\nA network trace on 2026-08-24 confirmed zero outbound telemetry traffic once the opt-out flag is set, closing the CLI-side verification as Completed.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Remaining Limitation\\n\\nThe third-party Electron crash reporter (Sentry) has not been audited for whether it independently respects the opt-out environment variable or requires its own disable hook for minidump uploads.\\n\\n*Note*: CLI-side telemetry opt-out is verified. Full privacy compliance for air-gapped/opt-out users cannot be claimed until the Sentry crash-reporter path is audited separately.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 opt out behaviour design the cli and api collect anonym usag metric page process ocr fallback rate to help tune the detect engin set cipher _ telemetri 0 or the equival gui toggl is design to immedi stop all outbound telemetri traffic to the metric endpoint sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 design time issu found and patch pend queue leak while design the flag semant test surfac that the opt out flag block network egress correct but the telemetrylogg kept write event payload to a local sqlite queue regardless that meant re enabl telemetri later would flush the entir backlog accumul dure the opt out period includ event the user believ were never be record the logger wa patch to a no op backend when opt out close that gap befor the flag semant were final sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 verif retrospect a network trace on 2026 08 24 confirm zero outbound telemetri traffic onc the opt out flag is set close the cli side verif a complet sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 remain limit the third parti electron crash report sentri ha not been audit for whether it independ respect the opt out environ variabl or requir it own disabl hook for minidump upload note cli side telemetri opt out is verifi full privaci complianc for air gap opt out user can not be claim until the sentri crash report path is audit separ\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9e43bb08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"id\": \"c3381a6a564a6c9c\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.38049023164233026, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2186163737747575, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7581959, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9e43bb08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1587, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:00:54\", \"token_count\": 503, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-08\\n\\n# Slack Thread: API Authentication Deferral\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-28\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-20\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 13:07] Bob**: Looking into REST API auth for v1.0. Do we need a full auth story now, or is trusted local network enough for the first release?\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 13:22] Diana**: Given the PII involved, something robust would be nice. But if this is strictly local-network-only, we might not need it for v1.0.\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 14:00] Bob**: Doing a short study either way — what we'd need if we keep auth in scope versus what we defer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-29 14:23] Diana**: If we defer, we should at least write down the v1.1 requirements so we don't lose them.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:01] Alice**: Team, we're falling behind on core engine work. I'm deferring the auth module to v1.1. For v1.0, the API assumes a trusted local network.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:19] Diana**: Manageable if we stay local-network-only. I'll note the deferral.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:21] Bob**: Fine. I'll keep the seams clean so adding auth later isn't a rewrite.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 11:04] Bob**: Still deferred — capturing v1.1 auth requirements while we remember them: REST auth with rotation support, since v1.0 is local-network-only.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 11:06] Diana**: Agreed. Folding that into the deferred-work notes so it survives until v1.1 planning.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 10:11] Alice**: Rechecked release scope for v1.0 — auth stays deferred to post-v1.0.0. Trusted-network assumption still holds.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 08 slack thread api authent deferr channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 28 last activ 2026 08 20 2026 06 28 13 07 bob look into rest api auth for v1 0 do we need a full auth stori now or is trust local network enough for the first releas 2026 06 28 13 22 diana given the pii involv someth robust would be nice but if this is strict local network onli we might not need it for v1 0 2026 06 28 14 00 bob do a short studi either way what we d need if we keep auth in scope versus what we defer 2026 06 29 14 23 diana if we defer we should at least write down the v1 1 requir so we don t lose them 2026 06 30 09 01 alic team we