 \"id\": \"fc6205e3092871f4\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.4596941037703902, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2991423939577003, \"vector_similarity\": 0.83431476, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-48-Telemetry-Opt-Out.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e96eb2508a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-48-Telemetry-Opt-Out.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-48-Telemetry-Opt-Out.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 826, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:38\", \"token_count\": 468, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-32\\n\\n# Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2032\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective decision note on the opt-out flag semantics settled 2026-08-20 for CIPH-48 (Telemetry Opt-Out).\\n\\n## Decision\\n\\nThe CLI accepts an explicit `--no-telemetry` flag. When present, it must suppress every outbound telemetry call for that invocation, including startup pings and error reports — not just usage-metric events.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-32\\n\\n# Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2032\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective decision note on the opt-out flag semantics settled 2026-08-20 for CIPH-48 (Telemetry Opt-Out).\\n\\n## Why \\\"explicit\\\" matters\\n\\nThe flag was deliberately specified as opt-out rather than opt-in-by-default-off, since the goal was to give privacy-sensitive users a clear, discoverable switch rather than relying on a config file most users would never find.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-32\\n\\n# Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2032\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective decision note on the opt-out flag semantics settled 2026-08-20 for CIPH-48 (Telemetry Opt-Out).\\n\\n## Note\\n\\nThis record settles the flag's expected behavior. Confirming that behavior against an actual network trace was a separate verification step and is not part of this decision note.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 32 telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2032 last updat 2026 09 06 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect decis note on the opt out flag semant settl 2026 08 20 for ciph 48 telemetri opt out decis the cli accept an explicit no telemetri flag when present it must suppress everi outbound telemetri call for that invoc includ startup ping and error report not just usag metric event sourc id src gdoc 32 telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2032 last updat 2026 09 06 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect decis note on the opt out flag semant settl 2026 08 20 for ciph 48 telemetri opt out whi explicit matter the flag wa deliber specifi a opt out rather than opt in by default off sinc the goal wa to give privaci sensit user a clear discover switch rather than reli on a config file most user would never find sourc id src gdoc 32 telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2032 last updat 2026 09 06 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect decis note on the opt out flag semant settl 2026 08 20 for ciph 48 telemetri opt out note this record settl the flag s expect behavior confirm that behavior against an actual network trace wa a separ verif step and is not part of this decis note\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9a043428a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-R