\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-11\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:16] Evan**: Finished the parser swap the audit flagged — pulled out the problem library and dropped in a replacement. Calling that step done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:18] Diana**: Nice turnaround. I'll fold it into the re-scan.\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:21] Charlie**: Did you check the new one's license closely, or just take the package listing at face value?\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 10:22] Evan**: Fair question — I should have looked harder before wiring it in.\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 09:54] Charlie**: Following up on this — since the replacement turned out to be AGPL, I'm searching for an Apache or MIT alternative that can do the same parsing.\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 09:56] Diana**: Any candidates yet?\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 09:58] Charlie**: A couple, but neither one covers everything the old library did. Still unresolved as of today — going to keep looking rather than force a bad fit.\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 10:22] Alice**: Let me know as soon as one of those candidates looks viable — don't want this dragging past the rest of the release work.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 41 slack thread licens parser swap channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 11 last activ 2026 08 15 2026 08 11 10 16 evan finish the parser swap the audit flag pull out the problem librari and drop in a replac call that step done 2026 08 11 1018 diana nice turnaround i ll fold it into the re scan 2026 08 11 10 21 charli did you check the new one s licens close or just take the packag list at face valu 2026 08 11 10 22 evan fair question i should have look harder befor wire it in 2026 08 15 09 54 charli follow up on this sinc the replac turn out to be agpl i m search for an apach or mit altern that can do the same pars 2026 08 15 09 56 diana ani candid yet 2026 08 15 09 58 charli a coupl but neither one cover everyth the old librari did still unresolv a of today go to keep look rather than forc a bad fit 2026 08 15 10 22 alic let me know a soon a one of those candid look viabl don t want this drag past the rest of the releas work\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8f4f0468a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"id\": \"2536eeff413cf064\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3585141937012183, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.19550071814459763, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73887897, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8f4f0468a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1186, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:17\", \"token_count\": 352, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\\nRetrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Scope of the 2026-08-09 inventory\\n\\nAn audit of the dependency tree was run to catalog every third-party license in use ahead of release, flagging anything more restrictive than a permissive license.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\\nRetrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Finding and immediate action\\n\\nThe PDF-parsing dependency's license was flagged as a concern, and the team swapped it for a different parser library as a direct result of this inventory.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\\nRetrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Status as of 2026-08-15\\n\\nBecause this report is written retrospectively on 2026-08-21, it can note the later developments: the replacement parser adopted from the 08-09 finding was swapped in on 2026-08-11, then the task reopened on 2026-08-12 when that replacement turned out itself to be AGPL-licensed, which is not acceptable for the shipped dependency set. By 2026-08-15 the team was searching for an Apache- or MIT-licensed alternative; that search had not concluded as of this writing.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 24 third parti licens inventori report owner diana document key doc 2024 last updat 2026 08 21 retrospect cover 2026 08 09 note status through 2026 08 15 retrospect report on the third parti licens audit under ciph 40 scope of the 2026 08 09 inventori an audit of the depend tree wa run to catalog everi third parti licens in use ahead of releas flag anyth more restrict than a permiss licens sourc id src gdoc 24 third parti licens inventori report owner diana document key doc 2024 last updat 2026 08 21 retrospect cover 2026 08 09 note status through 2026 08 15 retrospect report on the third parti licens audit under ciph 40 find and immedi action the pdf pars depend s licens wa flag a a concern and the team swap it for a differ parser librari a a direct result of this inventori sourc id src gdoc 24 third parti licens inventori report owner diana document key doc 2024 last updat 2026 08 21 retrospect cover 2026 08 09 note status through 2026 08 15 retrospect report on the third parti licens audit under ciph 40 status a of 2026 08 15 becaus this report is written retrospect on 2026 08 21 it can note the later develop the replac parser adopt from the 08 09 find wa swap in on 2026 08 11 then the task reopen on 2026 08 12 when that replac turn out itself to be agpl licens which is not accept for the ship depend set by 2026 08 15 the team wa search for an apach or mit licens altern that search had not conclud a of this write sourc id src gdoc 24 third parti licens inventori report owner diana document key doc 2024 last updat 2026 08 21 retrospect cover 2026 08 09 note status through 2026 08 15\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9a8a8848a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"id\": \"8e662b9dff3b4c7d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.35787545926849806, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17719690181214015, \"vector_similarity\": 0.77945876, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9a8a8848a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1278, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:48\", \"token_count\": 583, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \" - *Opened the task to build a centralized audit-trail system for tracking redaction activity across the pipeline.*\\n\\n- **2026-07-11**: Bob - Loader Refactor (Active)\\n\\n - *Refactored the document loader to prepare for streaming input ahead of hashing and audit capture.*\\n\\n- **2026-08-05**: Bob - SHA-256 Hashing (Active)\\n\\n - *Added SHA-256 hashing of input streams because the audit design requires an input hash alongside the redaction map.*\\n\\n- **2026-08-15**: Bob - Audit Schema Definition (Active)\\n\\n - *Defined the companion JSON audit schema (hash + redaction map) needed before CLI wiring.*\\n\\n- **2026-09-10**: Bob - CLI Integration (Active)\\n\\n - *Wired audit-log generation into the CLI path now that the schema was defined, to satisfy the release gate.*\\n\\n- **2026-09-18**: Diana - Audit Verify (Mismatch) (Active)\\n\\n - *Verification found the CLI-emitted audit records inconsistent with the defined schema; this mismatch remains an open release blocker.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"open the task to build a central audit trail system for track redact activ across the pipelin 2026 07 11 bob loader refactor activ refactor the document loader to prepar for stream input ahead of hash and audit captur 2026 08 05 bob sha 256 hash activ ad sha 256 hash of input stream becaus the audit design requir an input hash alongsid the redact map 2026 08 15 bob audit schema definit activ defin the companion json audit schema hash redact map need befor cli wire 2026 09 10 bob cli integr activ wire audit log generat into the cli path now that the schema wa defin to satisfi the releas gate 2026 09 18 diana audit verifi mismatch activ verif found the cli emit audit record inconsist with the defin schema this mismatch remain an open releas blocker\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e96d1e408a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-26-Audit-Trail-Logging.md\", \"id\": \"a015962ae73f1229\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.35554883926849806, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17719690181214015, \"vector_similarity\": 0.77170336, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-26-Audit-Trail-Logging.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e96d1e408a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-26-Audit-Trail-Logging.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-26-Audit-Trail-Logging.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 2011, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:38\", \"token_count\": 759, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"release blockers audit trail license compliance high DPI 2026-09-22\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"Beyond Docker/CVE and Windows signing, the remaining v1.0.0 compliance/audit holds are:\n\n| Item | Current status | Concrete defect/risk | Can engineering search alone close it? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Audit-trail logging (CIPH-26) | **Active; release blocker.** | CLI-generated audit records fail the defined JSON schema, undermining the SHA-256-hash/redaction-map audit trail as release evidence. | **Yes, in principle**—fix the record/schema mismatch and re-validate the emitted records. [SRC-CU-CIPH-26; SRC-MEET-10] |\n| Third-party license compliance (CIPH-40) | **Active (Reopened).** | The shipped PDF parsing/rasterization dependency chain still contains AGPL/copyleft software, unacceptable for the distribution model; the attempted replacement was also AGPL. | **No.** Search is only the first step: a suitable Apache/MIT alternative must be selected, integrated, and the full dependency tree re-audited. OCR model-data provenance is also still unverified. [SRC-CU-CIPH-40; SRC-GDOC-41] |\n| High-DPI PDF coordinate scaling (T036/CIPH-46) | **Blocked; treated as a pre-release gate.** | On scaled displays—especially complex PDFs with nested Form XObjects—preview/redaction coordinates misalign due to upstream rendering-library scaling math. | **No.** No safe local fix exists; closure requires an upstream correction or an accepted remediation/alternative-renderer decision. [SRC-MEET-10; SRC-GDOC-49; SRC-SLACK-58] |\n\nOne additional unresolved **privacy-compliance limitation** is Sentry/Electron crash reporting: CLI telemetry opt-out is verified, but the crash reporter has not been audited to confirm it honors opt-out or needs a separate minidump-disable hook. The dataset does **not** explicitly label this a v1.0.0 release gate, but it does say full opt-out/air-gapped privacy compliance cannot yet be claimed. Engineering search alone would not close it; it needs a behavior audit and possibly an implementation change. [SRC-GDOC-51]"}}
